    "### 6.1 Compare K = 3, 5, 7, 9 with 5-fold Cross-Validation\n",
    "We check if K = 5 is a reasonable choice.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Cross-validation uses the **training data only**. The test data is not touched.\n",
    "- Because the scaler is inside the pipeline, it is re-fitted in each fold (no leakage between folds).\n",
    "- We use the **F1 score** because only about 3.4% of samples are failures, so accuracy alone can look good even for a weak model.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is only a comparison. The main KNN model above stays at K = 5."
   ]
